## Purchases

`POST /purchases/verify` `{productId, source, receipt}` (signed in) asks the
store whether the purchase is genuine, records an entitlement and answers
`{valid}`. One purchase gives one entitlement: a receipt already used by
another account is refused. Other modules ask `has_entitlement(session,
user_id, product_id)` from `modules/purchases/public.py`.

- **Google Play** one-time products: set `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE` (a
  service account given access in Play Console → Users and permissions) and
  `ANDROID_PACKAGE_NAME`. Verified purchases are acknowledged, as Play
  requires within three days. Subscriptions need `purchases.subscriptionsv2`;
  add them to `GooglePlayVerifier`.
- **App Store:** not verified yet (503); implement `AppStoreVerifier.verify`
  with the App Store Server API.
